# Server Architecture (SoC)

## Layers (one job each)

| Layer | Folder | Allowed to do | Must NOT do |
|---|---|---|---|
| Routes | `routes/` | Wire path → middleware → controller | Business logic, DB |
| Controllers | `controllers/` | Parse req, call service, set status/cookies/json | DB queries, hashing, Cloudinary, matching rules |
| Services | `services/` | Business rules, orchestration, DB via models | `req`/`res`, Express types |
| Models | `models/` | Mongoose schemas + model export only | Business rules, HTTP |
| Types | `types/` | All shared TS types/interfaces | Runtime logic |
| Validators | `validators/` | Zod schemas only | Side effects |
| Middlewares | `middlewares/` | Cross-cutting HTTP (auth, upload, errors) | Domain business rules |
| Utils | `utils/` | Pure helpers (logger, AppError, tokens) | Feature orchestration |
| Config | `config/` | Env, DB, CORS, Cloudinary setup | Features |
| Socket | `socket/` | Connection lifecycle; call services | Fat business logic inline |

## Naming

Folder already states the role: `services/auth.ts`, not `auth.service.ts`.
Same for controllers, models, routes, validators, middlewares.

## Barrel `index.ts` files

Use selectively — **not** in every folder:

| Folder | `index.ts`? | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `routes/` | **Required** | `registerRoutes(app)` — **only** place that mounts feature routers |
| `types/` | **Required** | Re-export shared domain types |
| `services/` | Optional barrel | If present, prefer `from '../services/index.js'` |
| `middlewares/` | Optional barrel | If present, prefer `from '../middlewares/index.js'` |
| `controllers/`, `models/`, `validators/`, `config/`, `utils/`, `constants/` | **No** by default | Import the specific file |

When a barrel exists for middlewares/services, **use it** — don’t keep deep imports like `middlewares/auth.js` in routes.
### Routes registration

- File name: `routes/index.ts` — **not** `route.ts` / `routes.ts` (folder already means routes).
- Export `registerRoutes(app: Express): void`.
- New feature? Add `routes/foo.ts` **and** one line in `registerRoutes`. Do not mount routers in `app.ts`.

```ts
// ✅ app.ts
registerRoutes(app);

// ❌ app.ts
app.use('/api/auth', authRouter);
app.use('/api/chat', chatRouter);
```

### Nesting

Prefer domain nesting when a feature grows past ~1–2 files, e.g. `services/match/` in Phase 2. Do not nest for a single tiny file.

## Types

- Define domain/API types only under `server/src/types/`.
- Models import interfaces from `types/`; they do not export domain types.
- Controllers/services import types from `types/` (or `types/index.js`), never redefine shared inline shapes.
